<https://fhir-ig.digitalhealth.gov.ng/Basic/NgCoreRequestor> a fhir:Basic ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "NgCoreRequestor"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ActorDefinition NgCoreRequestor</b></p><a name=\"NgCoreRequestor\"> </a><a name=\"hcNgCoreRequestor\"> </a><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Actor: NgCoreRequestor </b></td><td>Nigeria Core Requestor</td><td>Type: system </td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\"><div><h3>Role</h3>\n<p>The <strong>Nigeria Core Requestor</strong> is an authorised application or service that\ninitiates interactions with a FHIR-enabled service.</p>\n<p>Examples include EMR/EHR systems, facility applications, mobile and community\nhealth applications, laboratory, pharmacy and imaging systems, program\nsystems, HIEs, registries, middleware, and reporting applications.</p>\n<h3>Responsibilities</h3>\n<p>A Requestor may:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>retrieve information using supported <code>read</code>, <code>search</code>, and other interactions;</li>\n<li>create, update, submit, or exchange FHIR resources and Bundles;</li>\n<li>invoke supported FHIR operations;</li>\n<li>query registry and terminology services;</li>\n<li>submit resources for validation or conformance testing; and</li>\n<li>process successful responses and <code>OperationOutcome</code> results.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Conformance expectations</h3>\n<p>A Requestor <strong>SHALL</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>construct requests conforming to applicable Nigeria Core profiles;</li>\n<li>provide mandatory and applicable <strong>Must Support</strong> elements;</li>\n<li>use governed identifiers and terminology where required;</li>\n<li>preserve required references and relationships;</li>\n<li>use only interactions and operations supported by the receiving service; and</li>\n<li>appropriately process FHIR responses and errors.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Requestor <strong>SHOULD</strong> inspect the receiving service's\n<code>CapabilityStatement</code> before relying on optional capabilities and <strong>SHALL NOT</strong>\nassume that every Responder supports every Nigeria Core resource, operation,\nsearch parameter, or program profile.</p>\n<p>Applicable national authentication, authorisation, privacy, consent, audit,\nand secure-exchange requirements <strong>SHALL</strong> be followed.</p>\n<h3>Relationships</h3>\n<p>The Requestor commonly interacts with the <strong>Nigeria Core Responder, Registry\nService, Terminology Service,</strong> and <strong>Conformance and Sandbox Service</strong>.</p>\n<p>A single implementation may perform multiple actor roles.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></div>"
  ] ;
